{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/699110-2ed-summon-the-hunt","id":699110,"title":"[2ed] Summon the hunt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-12T16:29:26-07:00","id":699110,"title":"[2ed] Summon the hunt","content":"Hi all,<br /> a couple of question needs your help if you can <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> First of all, using summon the hunt during a combat: how many turns does the summoned animals takes to arrive (for example a flock of crows)? And giving them the command to attack an enemy (after they drank the vitae) does this command become effective in the next turn right?<br /> And how can I quantify the damage (or the effect) of a flock of crows attacking an enemy?? Penality to the roll?? Damage?? <br /> Thank you all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 10-12-2015, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T06:19:11-07:00","id":699650,"title":"","content":"Isn't there no one who can give me an advice? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T06:38:37-07:00","id":699654,"title":"","content":"The time is not mentioned. If I were the ST, I'd make them arrive as fast as possible based on the animal type and distance with no supernatural speed. I'd give the Kindred a significant amount of leeway, like how they can restrict themself to a particular type of animal, I'd say they'd able to restrict the animals to arriving &quot;no sooner than&quot;, or even not acting before the rest arrive. If used after the start of a fight, with the turns short as they are, I'd say this particular ability is only useful if there are animals immediately nearby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T06:40:21-07:00","id":699657,"title":"","content":"How long they take to show up depends entirely on how far away they are at the time. Using it in the middle of a building will mean waiting longer than if you used it in the woods. <br /> <br /> Commanding said creatures requires Feral Whispers, so it will last as long as normal. You don't need to command them to attack anything that you spilled the blood on. They'll do that simply to get at the blood. <br /> <br /> The effects of being attacked by a swarm of crows is probably best modelled as if the vampire was using the Swarm Form merit on page 114. In other words, the victim gets the distracted condition and the swarm makes an appropriate strength + brawl roll each turn, ignoring defense. So probably 5, 6 dice? I dunno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T06:46:06-07:00","id":699661,"title":"","content":"There's no set time they could take to reach your destination, but a good rule of thumb is 6 turns-Successes (min 1 turn). For flocks of ravens and other swarms use the rules for swarms in the book as per the Swarm Form Merit (p.114). I would say that a swarm summoned by Call the Hunt would have a size equal to a vampire with Blood Potency equal to your successes in the activation roll. There's some stats for several animals in the Onyx Path Blog so you can check the Defense, Speed and attack pool of the swarms.<br /> <br /> A flock of crows or ravens, for example, would have a Speed 14 (fligth only) and attack rolling 2 dice (Strength 1+ Brawl 1), for Health you may use 4 health levels (those of a crow) for each point of effective Blood Potency (see above).<br /> <br /> And people tend to be slow to answer, take it easy<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T07:04:44-07:00","id":699677,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the suggestions. I had lost the swarm rules <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> And sorry for the hurry but I need to use this effect in my cronichle tonight <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T09:45:21-07:00","id":699903,"title":"","content":"If you have Demon: the Descent, it has the swarm rules in the form of a Tilt on page 179. I find it a little more concise than the Swarm Form Merit rules, though functionally they are pretty much the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2